{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhP1CdLTELW2GABVdVv4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Hp2ACUR52FGi1QeakD7R9T","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"for f in README.md .handwork/settings.json src/app.ts src/auth/*.ts src/cache/*.ts src/db/*.ts src/http/*.ts src/routes/*.ts src/seed.ts src/services/*.ts src/types.ts tests/*.ts; do echo \"=== $f\"; cat -n $f; done","description":"Print all source and test files"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":424,"cache_read_input_tokens":7796,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":424},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0143151f-222a-4d13-91f2-1dcef4d2e46b","uuid":"0e463aa2-6099-4a98-acf1-68ce60cc3779","timestamp":"2026-10-04T14:47:45.771Z","request_id":"req_011CfhP1CNTLDGmdtYNym9Xh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Hp2ACUR52FGi1QeakD7R9T":{"command":"for f in README.md .handwork/settings.json src/app.ts src/auth/*.ts src/cache/*.ts src/db/*.ts src/http/*.ts src/routes/*.ts src/seed.ts src/services/*.ts src/types.ts tests/*.ts; do echo \"=== $f\"; cat -n $f; done","description":"Print all source and test files"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hp2ACUR52FGi1QeakD7R9T","type":"tool_result","content":"=== README.md\n     1\t# Project-management API\n     2\t\n     3\tNode 24 runs TypeScript directly. Run `npm test`; no third-party dependencies are needed.\n     4\t\n     5\t`createApp(seed, cache?)` returns a synchronous `request({method,path,token?,query?,body?})` dispatcher plus the in-memory `db` and injected `cache`. The fixture uses no network, clock or database service. Database counters expose project reads, list queries and updates for instrumentation. Cache values are snapshots, not references into storage.\n     6\t\n     7\t## API conventions\n     8\t\n     9\t- Successful reads and updates return status 200 with the resource, or a list `{items,total,page,pageSize,sort,direction}`. Logout returns 204 with null.\n    10\t- Missing/invalid sessions return 401 `{error:\"unauthorized\"}`.\n    11\t- Authenticated nonmembers return 403 `{error:\"forbidden\"}` with no resource fields. Known project IDs use the project's actual owning organization, regardless of organization IDs supplied in query/body. Only `name` is editable; ownership cannot be reassigned.\n    12\t- Missing projects return 404 `{error:\"not_found\"}`. Unknown routes also return 404.\n    13\t- Invalid list options return 400 `{error:\"invalid_query\"}`; invalid project names return 400 `{error:\"invalid_body\"}`. Unexpected failures return 500 `{error:\"internal_error\"}`.\n    14\t\n    15\tGET/PATCH `/projects/:projectId` require membership in the project's owning organization. GET `/organizations/:organizationId/projects` requires current membership, including on cache hits. GET `/organizations` lists the current user's organizations; GET `/organizations/:organizationId`, GET `/me`, DELETE `/session`, and GET `/health` also work.\n    16\t\n    17\t## Lists and caching\n    18\t\n    19\tPage and pageSize default to 1 and 10 (positive integers, size at most 100). Sort is name or updatedAt (default name); direction is asc or desc (default asc). Ties sort by ID in the same direction. The cache must keep organizations, pages, page sizes, sort fields and directions distinct. A successful project update invalidates every list variant for only the owning organization; unrelated cached lists must remain usable. Unauthorized requests must not mutate storage or cached entries. Revoked membership takes effect immediately. Caching must remain enabled, with repeated identical authorized lists avoiding another repository list query.\n    20\t\n    21\tThe injected cache interface is get/set/delete/keys; callers may supply an instrumented implementation. Organization IDs are opaque strings, so cache grouping must distinguish IDs that share prefixes or contain punctuation.\n=== .handwork/settings.json\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"provider\": \"codex\",\n     3\t  \"models\": {\n     4\t    \"codex\": \"gpt-6-astra\"\n     5\t  },\n     6\t  \"effort\": \"low\",\n     7\t  \"fast_mode\": false\n     8\t}\n=== src/app.ts\n     1\timport { createDatabase } from './db/database.ts';\n     2\timport type { Seed } from './db/database.ts';\n     3\timport { createCache } from './cache/project-cache.ts';\n     4\timport type { Cache } from './cache/project-cache.ts';\n     5\timport { createRouter } from './http/router.ts';\n     6\timport { registerProjects } from './routes/projects.ts';\n     7\timport { registerOrganizations } from './routes/organizations.ts';\n     8\timport { registerAccount } from './routes/account.ts';\n     9\texport function createApp(seed:Seed,cache:Cache=createCache()) {\n    10\t  const db=createDatabase(seed),router=createRouter();\n    11\t  registerProjects(router,db,cache);registerOrganizations(router,db);registerAccount(router,db);\n    12\t  return {request:router.handle,db,cache};\n    13\t}\n=== src/auth/membership.ts\n     1\timport { membershipRepository } from '../db/membership-repository.ts';\n     2\timport type { Database } from '../db/database.ts';\n     3\timport { HttpError } from '../http/response.ts';\n     4\texport function requireMembership(db:Database,userId:string,organizationId:string) {\n     5\t  if(!membershipRepository(db).has(userId,organizationId)) throw new HttpError(403,'forbidden');\n     6\t}\n=== src/auth/session.ts\n     1\timport type { Database } from '../db/database.ts';\n     2\timport { HttpError } from '../http/response.ts';\n     3\texport function requireSession(db:Database,token?:string) {\n     4\t  const id=token ? db.sessions.get(token) : undefined;\n     5\t  const user=id ? db.users.get(id) : undefined;\n     6\t  if(!user) throw new HttpError(401,'unauthorized');\n     7\t  return {...user};\n     8\t}\n=== src/cache/keys.ts\n     1\timport type { ListOptions } from '../types.ts';\n     2\texport function projectListKey(organizationId:string,options:ListOptions):string {\n     3\t  return `projects:list:${options.page}:${options.pageSize}:${options.sort}:${options.direction}`;\n     4\t}\n     5\texport function projectDetailKey(projectId:string):string { return `projects:detail:${projectId}`; }\n=== src/cache/project-cache.ts\n     1\texport interface Cache {\n     2\t  get(key:string): unknown;\n     3\t  set(key:string,value:unknown): void;\n     4\t  delete(key:string): void;\n     5\t  keys(): string[];\n     6\t}\n     7\texport function createCache() {\n     8\t  const entries=new Map<string,unknown>();\n     9\t  const metrics={hits:0,misses:0,writes:0,deletes:0};\n    10\t  return {\n    11\t    metrics,\n    12\t    get(key:string){if(entries.has(key)){metrics.hits++;return structuredClone(entries.get(key));}metrics.misses++;return undefined;},\n    13\t    set(key:string,value:unknown){metrics.writes++;entries.set(key,structuredClone(value));},\n    14\t    delete(key:string){metrics.deletes++;entries.delete(key);},\n    15\t    keys(){return [...entries.keys()];},\n    16\t  };\n    17\t}\n=== src/db/database.ts\n     1\timport type { Project, Organization, User } from '../types.ts';\n     2\texport type Seed = { projects: Project[]; organizations: Organization[]; users: User[]; memberships: {userId:string; organizationId:string}[]; sessions: Record<string,string> };\n     3\texport function createDatabase(seed: Seed) {\n     4\t  return {\n     5\t    projects: new Map(seed.projects.map(p => [p.id, structuredClone(p)])),\n     6\t    organizations: new Map(seed.organizations.map(o => [o.id, {...o}])),\n     7\t    users: new Map(seed.users.map(u => [u.id, {...u}])),\n     8\t    memberships: new Set(seed.memberships.map(m => JSON.stringify([m.userId,m.organizationId]))),\n     9\t    sessions: new Map(Object.entries(seed.sessions)),\n    10\t    counters: { projectReads: 0, projectLists: 0, projectUpdates: 0 },\n    11\t  };\n    12\t}\n    13\texport type Database = ReturnType<typeof createDatabase>;\n=== src/db/membership-repository.ts\n     1\timport type { Database } from './database.ts';\n     2\texport function membershipRepository(db:Database) {\n     3\t  const key=(userId:string,organizationId:string)=>JSON.stringify([userId,organizationId]);\n     4\t  return {\n     5\t    has(userId:string,organizationId:string){return db.memberships.has(key(userId,organizationId));},\n     6\t    revoke(userId:string,organizationId:string){db.memberships.delete(key(userId,organizationId));},\n     7\t    organizationsFor(userId:string){return [...db.organizations.values()].filter(o=>db.memberships.has(key(userId,o.id))).map(o=>({...o}));},\n     8\t  };\n     9\t}\n=== src/db/project-repository.ts\n     1\timport type { Database } from './database.ts';\n     2\timport type { ListOptions } from '../types.ts';\n     3\texport function projectRepository(db: Database) {\n     4\t  return {\n     5\t    find(id: string) { db.counters.projectReads++; const p=db.projects.get(id); return p ? {...p} : undefined; },\n     6\t    list(organizationId: string, options: ListOptions) {\n     7\t      db.counters.projectLists++;\n     8\t      const rows=[...db.projects.values()].filter(p=>p.organizationId===organizationId);\n     9\t      rows.sort((a,b)=> {\n    10\t        const primary=options.sort==='name' ? a.name.localeCompare(b.name) : a.updatedAt-b.updatedAt;\n    11\t        return (primary || a.id.localeCompare(b.id)) * (options.direction==='asc' ? 1 : -1);\n    12\t      });\n    13\t      const start=(options.page-1)*options.pageSize;\n    14\t      return { items: rows.slice(start,start+options.pageSize).map(p=>({...p})), total: rows.length, ...options };\n    15\t    },\n    16\t    update(id:string, name:string) {\n    17\t      db.counters.projectUpdates++;\n    18\t      const p=db.projects.get(id); if(!p) return undefined;\n    19\t      const updated={...p,name,updatedAt:p.updatedAt+1}; db.projects.set(id,updated); return {...updated};\n    20\t    },\n    21\t  };\n    22\t}\n=== src/http/list-options.ts\n     1\timport type { ListOptions } from '../types.ts';\n     2\timport { HttpError } from './response.ts';\n     3\texport function listOptions(query:Record<string,string>={}):ListOptions {\n     4\t  const page=Number(query.page??1),pageSize=Number(query.pageSize??10),sort=query.sort??'name',direction=query.direction??'asc';\n     5\t  if(!Number.isInteger(page)||page<1||!Number.isInteger(pageSize)||pageSize<1||pageSize>100||!['name','updatedAt'].includes(sort)||!['asc','desc'].includes(direction))throw new HttpError(400,'invalid_query');\n     6\t  return {page,pageSize,sort:sort as ListOptions['sort'],direction:direction as ListOptions['direction']};\n     7\t}\n=== src/http/response.ts\n     1\timport type { Response } from '../types.ts';\n     2\texport class HttpError extends Error {\n     3\t  status:number;\n     4\t  constructor(status:number,message:string){super(message);this.status=status;}\n     5\t}\n     6\texport function ok(body:unknown):Response{return {status:200,body};}\n     7\texport function failure(error:unknown):Response {\n     8\t  return error instanceof HttpError ? {status:error.status,body:{error:error.message}} : {status:500,body:{error:'internal_error'}};\n     9\t}\n=== src/http/router.ts\n     1\timport type { Request, Response } from '../types.ts';\n     2\timport { failure, HttpError } from './response.ts';\n     3\texport type Handler=(request:Request,params:Record<string,string>)=>Response;\n     4\texport function createRouter() {\n     5\t  const routes:{method:string;pattern:string[];handler:Handler}[]=[];\n     6\t  return {\n     7\t    add(method:string,path:string,handler:Handler){routes.push({method,pattern:path.split('/').filter(Boolean),handler});},\n     8\t    handle(request:Request):Response {\n     9\t      try {\n    10\t        const path=request.path.split('/').filter(Boolean);\n    11\t        for(const route of routes){\n    12\t          if(route.method!==request.method || route.pattern.length!==path.length) continue;\n    13\t          const params:Record<string,string>={};\n    14\t          if(!route.pattern.every((part,i)=>part.startsWith(':') ? (params[part.slice(1)]=decodeURIComponent(path[i]),true) : part===path[i])) continue;\n    15\t          return route.handler(request,params);\n    16\t        }\n    17\t        throw new HttpError(404,'not_found');\n    18\t      } catch(error){return failure(error);}\n    19\t    },\n    20\t  };\n    21\t}\n    22\texport type Router=ReturnType<typeof createRouter>;\n=== src/routes/account.ts\n     1\timport type { Router } from '../http/router.ts';\n     2\timport type { Database } from '../db/database.ts';\n     3\timport { requireSession } from '../auth/session.ts';\n     4\timport { ok } from '../http/response.ts';\n     5\texport function registerAccount(router:Router,db:Database) {\n     6\t  router.add('GET','/health',()=>ok({status:'ok'}));\n     7\t  router.add('GET','/me',req=>ok(requireSession(db,req.token)));\n     8\t  router.add('DELETE','/session',req=>{requireSession(db,req.token);db.sessions.delete(req.token!);return {status:204,body:null};});\n     9\t}\n=== src/routes/organizations.ts\n     1\timport type { Router } from '../http/router.ts';\n     2\timport type { Database } from '../db/database.ts';\n     3\timport { requireSession } from '../auth/session.ts';\n     4\timport { organizationService } from '../services/organization-service.ts';\n     5\timport { ok } from '../http/response.ts';\n     6\texport function registerOrganizations(router:Router,db:Database) {\n     7\t  const service=organizationService(db);\n     8\t  router.add('GET','/organizations',(req)=>ok(service.list(requireSession(db,req.token).id)));\n     9\t  router.add('GET','/organizations/:organizationId',(req,p)=>ok(service.detail(requireSession(db,req.token).id,p.organizationId)));\n    10\t}\n=== src/routes/projects.ts\n     1\timport type { Router } from '../http/router.ts';\n     2\timport type { Database } from '../db/database.ts';\n     3\timport type { Cache } from '../cache/project-cache.ts';\n     4\timport { requireSession } from '../auth/session.ts';\n     5\timport { projectService } from '../services/project-service.ts';\n     6\timport { listOptions } from '../http/list-options.ts';\n     7\timport { ok } from '../http/response.ts';\n     8\texport function registerProjects(router:Router,db:Database,cache:Cache) {\n     9\t  const service=projectService(db,cache);\n    10\t  router.add('GET','/projects/:projectId',(req,p)=>ok(service.detail(requireSession(db,req.token).id,p.projectId)));\n    11\t  router.add('PATCH','/projects/:projectId',(req,p)=>ok(service.update(requireSession(db,req.token).id,p.projectId,req.body)));\n    12\t  router.add('GET','/organizations/:organizationId/projects',(req,p)=>ok(service.list(requireSession(db,req.token).id,p.organizationId,listOptions(req.query))));\n    13\t}\n=== src/seed.ts\n     1\timport type { Seed } from './db/database.ts';\n     2\texport function sampleSeed():Seed {return {\n     3\t  users:[{id:'alice',name:'Alice'},{id:'bob',name:'Bob'},{id:'both',name:'Both'}],\n     4\t  organizations:[{id:'org-a',name:'A'},{id:'org-b',name:'B'}],\n     5\t  memberships:[{userId:'alice',organizationId:'org-a'},{userId:'bob',organizationId:'org-b'},{userId:'both',organizationId:'org-a'},{userId:'both',organizationId:'org-b'}],\n     6\t  sessions:{alice:'alice',bob:'bob',both:'both'},\n     7\t  projects:[{id:'a1',organizationId:'org-a',name:'Alpha',updatedAt:3},{id:'a2',organizationId:'org-a',name:'Delta',updatedAt:1},{id:'a3',organizationId:'org-a',name:'Gamma',updatedAt:2},{id:'b1',organizationId:'org-b',name:'Beta',updatedAt:7},{id:'b2',organizationId:'org-b',name:'Echo',updatedAt:5},{id:'b3',organizationId:'org-b',name:'Foxtrot',updatedAt:6}],\n     8\t};}\n=== src/services/organization-service.ts\n     1\timport type { Database } from '../db/database.ts';\n     2\timport { membershipRepository } from '../db/membership-repository.ts';\n     3\timport { requireMembership } from '../auth/membership.ts';\n     4\timport { HttpError } from '../http/response.ts';\n     5\texport function organizationService(db:Database){return {\n     6\t  list(userId:string){return {items:membershipRepository(db).organizationsFor(userId)};},\n     7\t  detail(userId:string,id:string){requireMembership(db,userId,id);const org=db.organizations.get(id);if(!org)throw new HttpError(404,'not_found');return {...org};},\n     8\t};}\n=== src/services/project-service.ts\n     1\timport type { Database } from '../db/database.ts';\n     2\timport type { Cache } from '../cache/project-cache.ts';\n     3\timport type { ListOptions } from '../types.ts';\n     4\timport { projectRepository } from '../db/project-repository.ts';\n     5\timport { requireMembership } from '../auth/membership.ts';\n     6\timport { projectListKey, projectDetailKey } from '../cache/keys.ts';\n     7\timport { HttpError } from '../http/response.ts';\n     8\texport function projectService(db:Database,cache:Cache) {\n     9\t  const projects=projectRepository(db);\n    10\t  function detail(userId:string,projectId:string) {\n    11\t    const project=projects.find(projectId);\n    12\t    if(!project)throw new HttpError(404,'not_found');\n    13\t    return project;\n    14\t  }\n    15\t  return {\n    16\t    detail,\n    17\t    list(userId:string,organizationId:string,options:ListOptions) {\n    18\t      requireMembership(db,userId,organizationId);\n    19\t      const key=projectListKey(organizationId,options);\n    20\t      const cached=cache.get(key);\n    21\t      if(cached!==undefined)return cached;\n    22\t      const result=projects.list(organizationId,options);cache.set(key,result);return result;\n    23\t    },\n    24\t    update(userId:string,projectId:string,body:unknown) {\n    25\t      detail(userId,projectId);\n    26\t      if(!body||typeof body!=='object'||typeof (body as any).name!=='string'||!(body as any).name.trim())throw new HttpError(400,'invalid_body');\n    27\t      const updated=projects.update(projectId,(body as any).name.trim())!;\n    28\t      cache.delete(projectDetailKey(projectId));\n    29\t      return updated;\n    30\t    },\n    31\t  };\n    32\t}\n=== src/types.ts\n     1\texport type Project = { id: string; organizationId: string; name: string; updatedAt: number };\n     2\texport type Organization = { id: string; name: string };\n     3\texport type User = { id: string; name: string };\n     4\texport type ListOptions = { page: number; pageSize: number; sort: 'name' | 'updatedAt'; direction: 'asc' | 'desc' };\n     5\texport type Request = { method: string; path: string; token?: string; query?: Record<string,string>; body?: unknown };\n     6\texport type Response = { status: number; body: unknown };\n=== tests/account.test.ts\n     1\timport test from 'node:test';\n     2\timport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n     3\timport { createApp } from '../src/app.ts';\n     4\timport { sampleSeed } from '../src/seed.ts';\n     5\ttest('health and profile',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());assert.deepEqual(a.request({method:'GET',path:'/health'}).body,{status:'ok'});assert.equal((a.request({method:'GET',path:'/me',token:'alice'}).body as any).id,'alice');});\n     6\ttest('organizations scoped to user',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());assert.deepEqual((a.request({method:'GET',path:'/organizations',token:'alice'}).body as any).items.map((o:any)=>o.id),['org-a']);});\n     7\ttest('logout revokes session',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());assert.equal(a.request({method:'DELETE',path:'/session',token:'alice'}).status,204);assert.equal(a.request({method:'GET',path:'/me',token:'alice'}).status,401);});\n=== tests/projects.test.ts\n     1\timport test from 'node:test';\n     2\timport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n     3\timport { createApp } from '../src/app.ts';\n     4\timport { sampleSeed } from '../src/seed.ts';\n     5\ttest('authenticated detail',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());assert.equal(a.request({method:'GET',path:'/projects/a1',token:'alice'}).status,200);});\n     6\ttest('authenticated list',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());const r=a.request({method:'GET',path:'/organizations/org-a/projects',token:'alice'});assert.equal(r.status,200);assert.equal((r.body as any).items.length,3);});\n     7\ttest('update then read',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());assert.equal(a.request({method:'PATCH',path:'/projects/a1',token:'alice',body:{name:'New'}}).status,200);assert.equal((a.request({method:'GET',path:'/projects/a1',token:'alice'}).body as any).name,'New');});\n     8\ttest('anonymous request rejected',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());assert.deepEqual(a.request({method:'GET',path:'/projects/a1'}),{status:401,body:{error:'unauthorized'}});});\n     9\ttest('invalid update rejected',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());assert.equal(a.request({method:'PATCH',path:'/projects/a1',token:'alice',body:{name:''}}).status,400);});","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0143151f-222a-4d13-91f2-1dcef4d2e46b","uuid":"78ce18fb-4041-47dc-9074-dd14a7d1ef85","timestamp":"2026-10-04T14:47:45.829Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== README.md\n     1\t# Project-management API\n     2\t\n     3\tNode 24 runs TypeScript directly. Run `npm test`; no third-party dependencies are needed.\n     4\t\n     5\t`createApp(seed, cache?)` returns a synchronous `request({method,path,token?,query?,body?})` dispatcher plus the in-memory `db` and injected `cache`. The fixture uses no network, clock or database service. Database counters expose project reads, list queries and updates for instrumentation. Cache values are snapshots, not references into storage.\n     6\t\n     7\t## API conventions\n     8\t\n     9\t- Successful reads and updates return status 200 with the resource, or a list `{items,total,page,pageSize,sort,direction}`. Logout returns 204 with null.\n    10\t- Missing/invalid sessions return 401 `{error:\"unauthorized\"}`.\n    11\t- Authenticated nonmembers return 403 `{error:\"forbidden\"}` with no resource fields. Known project IDs use the project's actual owning organization, regardless of organization IDs supplied in query/body. Only `name` is editable; ownership cannot be reassigned.\n    12\t- Missing projects return 404 `{error:\"not_found\"}`. Unknown routes also return 404.\n    13\t- Invalid list options return 400 `{error:\"invalid_query\"}`; invalid project names return 400 `{error:\"invalid_body\"}`. Unexpected failures return 500 `{error:\"internal_error\"}`.\n    14\t\n    15\tGET/PATCH `/projects/:projectId` require membership in the project's owning organization. GET `/organizations/:organizationId/projects` requires current membership, including on cache hits. GET `/organizations` lists the current user's organizations; GET `/organizations/:organizationId`, GET `/me`, DELETE `/session`, and GET `/health` also work.\n    16\t\n    17\t## Lists and caching\n    18\t\n    19\tPage and pageSize default to 1 and 10 (positive integers, size at most 100). Sort is name or updatedAt (default name); direction is asc or desc (default asc). Ties sort by ID in the same direction. The cache must keep organizations, pages, page sizes, sort fields and directions distinct. A successful project update invalidates every list variant for only the owning organization; unrelated cached lists must remain usable. Unauthorized requests must not mutate storage or cached entries. Revoked membership takes effect immediately. Caching must remain enabled, with repeated identical authorized lists avoiding another repository list query.\n    20\t\n    21\tThe injected cache interface is get/set/delete/keys; callers may supply an instrumented implementation. Organization IDs are opaque strings, so cache grouping must distinguish IDs that share prefixes or contain punctuation.\n=== .handwork/settings.json\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"provider\": \"codex\",\n     3\t  \"models\": {\n     4\t    \"codex\": \"gpt-6-astra\"\n     5\t  },\n     6\t  \"effort\": \"low\",\n     7\t  \"fast_mode\": false\n     8\t}\n=== src/app.ts\n     1\timport { createDatabase } from './db/database.ts';\n     2\timport type { Seed } from './db/database.ts';\n     3\timport { createCache } from './cache/project-cache.ts';\n     4\timport type { Cache } from './cache/project-cache.ts';\n     5\timport { createRouter } from './http/router.ts';\n     6\timport { registerProjects } from './routes/projects.ts';\n     7\timport { registerOrganizations } from './routes/organizations.ts';\n     8\timport { registerAccount } from './routes/account.ts';\n     9\texport function createApp(seed:Seed,cache:Cache=createCache()) {\n    10\t  const db=createDatabase(seed),router=createRouter();\n    11\t  registerProjects(router,db,cache);registerOrganizations(router,db);registerAccount(router,db);\n    12\t  return {request:router.handle,db,cache};\n    13\t}\n=== src/auth/membership.ts\n     1\timport { membershipRepository } from '../db/membership-repository.ts';\n     2\timport type { Database } from '../db/database.ts';\n     3\timport { HttpError } from '../http/response.ts';\n     4\texport function requireMembership(db:Database,userId:string,organizationId:string) {\n     5\t  if(!membershipRepository(db).has(userId,organizationId)) throw new HttpError(403,'forbidden');\n     6\t}\n=== src/auth/session.ts\n     1\timport type { Database } from '../db/database.ts';\n     2\timport { HttpError } from '../http/response.ts';\n     3\texport function requireSession(db:Database,token?:string) {\n     4\t  const id=token ? db.sessions.get(token) : undefined;\n     5\t  const user=id ? db.users.get(id) : undefined;\n     6\t  if(!user) throw new HttpError(401,'unauthorized');\n     7\t  return {...user};\n     8\t}\n=== src/cache/keys.ts\n     1\timport type { ListOptions } from '../types.ts';\n     2\texport function projectListKey(organizationId:string,options:ListOptions):string {\n     3\t  return `projects:list:${options.page}:${options.pageSize}:${options.sort}:${options.direction}`;\n     4\t}\n     5\texport function projectDetailKey(projectId:string):string { return `projects:detail:${projectId}`; }\n=== src/cache/project-cache.ts\n     1\texport interface Cache {\n     2\t  get(key:string): unknown;\n     3\t  set(key:string,value:unknown): void;\n     4\t  delete(key:string): void;\n     5\t  keys(): string[];\n     6\t}\n     7\texport function createCache() {\n     8\t  const entries=new Map<string,unknown>();\n     9\t  const metrics={hits:0,misses:0,writes:0,deletes:0};\n    10\t  return {\n    11\t    metrics,\n    12\t    get(key:string){if(entries.has(key)){metrics.hits++;return structuredClone(entries.get(key));}metrics.misses++;return undefined;},\n    13\t    set(key:string,value:unknown){metrics.writes++;entries.set(key,structuredClone(value));},\n    14\t    delete(key:string){metrics.deletes++;entries.delete(key);},\n    15\t    keys(){return [...entries.keys()];},\n    16\t  };\n    17\t}\n=== src/db/database.ts\n     1\timport type { Project, Organization, User } from '../types.ts';\n     2\texport type Seed = { projects: Project[]; organizations: Organization[]; users: User[]; memberships: {userId:string; organizationId:string}[]; sessions: Record<string,string> };\n     3\texport function createDatabase(seed: Seed) {\n     4\t  return {\n     5\t    projects: new Map(seed.projects.map(p => [p.id, structuredClone(p)])),\n     6\t    organizations: new Map(seed.organizations.map(o => [o.id, {...o}])),\n     7\t    users: new Map(seed.users.map(u => [u.id, {...u}])),\n     8\t    memberships: new Set(seed.memberships.map(m => JSON.stringify([m.userId,m.organizationId]))),\n     9\t    sessions: new Map(Object.entries(seed.sessions)),\n    10\t    counters: { projectReads: 0, projectLists: 0, projectUpdates: 0 },\n    11\t  };\n    12\t}\n    13\texport type Database = ReturnType<typeof createDatabase>;\n=== src/db/membership-repository.ts\n     1\timport type { Database } from './database.ts';\n     2\texport function membershipRepository(db:Database) {\n     3\t  const key=(userId:string,organizationId:string)=>JSON.stringify([userId,organizationId]);\n     4\t  return {\n     5\t    has(userId:string,organizationId:string){return db.memberships.has(key(userId,organizationId));},\n     6\t    revoke(userId:string,organizationId:string){db.memberships.delete(key(userId,organizationId));},\n     7\t    organizationsFor(userId:string){return [...db.organizations.values()].filter(o=>db.memberships.has(key(userId,o.id))).map(o=>({...o}));},\n     8\t  };\n     9\t}\n=== src/db/project-repository.ts\n     1\timport type { Database } from './database.ts';\n     2\timport type { ListOptions } from '../types.ts';\n     3\texport function projectRepository(db: Database) {\n     4\t  return {\n     5\t    find(id: string) { db.counters.projectReads++; const p=db.projects.get(id); return p ? {...p} : undefined; },\n     6\t    list(organizationId: string, options: ListOptions) {\n     7\t      db.counters.projectLists++;\n     8\t      const rows=[...db.projects.values()].filter(p=>p.organizationId===organizationId);\n     9\t      rows.sort((a,b)=> {\n    10\t        const primary=options.sort==='name' ? a.name.localeCompare(b.name) : a.updatedAt-b.updatedAt;\n    11\t        return (primary || a.id.localeCompare(b.id)) * (options.direction==='asc' ? 1 : -1);\n    12\t      });\n    13\t      const start=(options.page-1)*options.pageSize;\n    14\t      return { items: rows.slice(start,start+options.pageSize).map(p=>({...p})), total: rows.length, ...options };\n    15\t    },\n    16\t    update(id:string, name:string) {\n    17\t      db.counters.projectUpdates++;\n    18\t      const p=db.projects.get(id); if(!p) return undefined;\n    19\t      const updated={...p,name,updatedAt:p.updatedAt+1}; db.projects.set(id,updated); return {...updated};\n    20\t    },\n    21\t  };\n    22\t}\n=== src/http/list-options.ts\n     1\timport type { ListOptions } from '../types.ts';\n     2\timport { HttpError } from './response.ts';\n     3\texport function listOptions(query:Record<string,string>={}):ListOptions {\n     4\t  const page=Number(query.page??1),pageSize=Number(query.pageSize??10),sort=query.sort??'name',direction=query.direction??'asc';\n     5\t  if(!Number.isInteger(page)||page<1||!Number.isInteger(pageSize)||pageSize<1||pageSize>100||!['name','updatedAt'].includes(sort)||!['asc','desc'].includes(direction))throw new HttpError(400,'invalid_query');\n     6\t  return {page,pageSize,sort:sort as ListOptions['sort'],direction:direction as ListOptions['direction']};\n     7\t}\n=== src/http/response.ts\n     1\timport type { Response } from '../types.ts';\n     2\texport class HttpError extends Error {\n     3\t  status:number;\n     4\t  constructor(status:number,message:string){super(message);this.status=status;}\n     5\t}\n     6\texport function ok(body:unknown):Response{return {status:200,body};}\n     7\texport function failure(error:unknown):Response {\n     8\t  return error instanceof HttpError ? {status:error.status,body:{error:error.message}} : {status:500,body:{error:'internal_error'}};\n     9\t}\n=== src/http/router.ts\n     1\timport type { Request, Response } from '../types.ts';\n     2\timport { failure, HttpError } from './response.ts';\n     3\texport type Handler=(request:Request,params:Record<string,string>)=>Response;\n     4\texport function createRouter() {\n     5\t  const routes:{method:string;pattern:string[];handler:Handler}[]=[];\n     6\t  return {\n     7\t    add(method:string,path:string,handler:Handler){routes.push({method,pattern:path.split('/').filter(Boolean),handler});},\n     8\t    handle(request:Request):Response {\n     9\t      try {\n    10\t        const path=request.path.split('/').filter(Boolean);\n    11\t        for(const route of routes){\n    12\t          if(route.method!==request.method || route.pattern.length!==path.length) continue;\n    13\t          const params:Record<string,string>={};\n    14\t          if(!route.pattern.every((part,i)=>part.startsWith(':') ? (params[part.slice(1)]=decodeURIComponent(path[i]),true) : part===path[i])) continue;\n    15\t          return route.handler(request,params);\n    16\t        }\n    17\t        throw new HttpError(404,'not_found');\n    18\t      } catch(error){return failure(error);}\n    19\t    },\n    20\t  };\n    21\t}\n    22\texport type Router=ReturnType<typeof createRouter>;\n=== src/routes/account.ts\n     1\timport type { Router } from '../http/router.ts';\n     2\timport type { Database } from '../db/database.ts';\n     3\timport { requireSession } from '../auth/session.ts';\n     4\timport { ok } from '../http/response.ts';\n     5\texport function registerAccount(router:Router,db:Database) {\n     6\t  router.add('GET','/health',()=>ok({status:'ok'}));\n     7\t  router.add('GET','/me',req=>ok(requireSession(db,req.token)));\n     8\t  router.add('DELETE','/session',req=>{requireSession(db,req.token);db.sessions.delete(req.token!);return {status:204,body:null};});\n     9\t}\n=== src/routes/organizations.ts\n     1\timport type { Router } from '../http/router.ts';\n     2\timport type { Database } from '../db/database.ts';\n     3\timport { requireSession } from '../auth/session.ts';\n     4\timport { organizationService } from '../services/organization-service.ts';\n     5\timport { ok } from '../http/response.ts';\n     6\texport function registerOrganizations(router:Router,db:Database) {\n     7\t  const service=organizationService(db);\n     8\t  router.add('GET','/organizations',(req)=>ok(service.list(requireSession(db,req.token).id)));\n     9\t  router.add('GET','/organizations/:organizationId',(req,p)=>ok(service.detail(requireSession(db,req.token).id,p.organizationId)));\n    10\t}\n=== src/routes/projects.ts\n     1\timport type { Router } from '../http/router.ts';\n     2\timport type { Database } from '../db/database.ts';\n     3\timport type { Cache } from '../cache/project-cache.ts';\n     4\timport { requireSession } from '../auth/session.ts';\n     5\timport { projectService } from '../services/project-service.ts';\n     6\timport { listOptions } from '../http/list-options.ts';\n     7\timport { ok } from '../http/response.ts';\n     8\texport function registerProjects(router:Router,db:Database,cache:Cache) {\n     9\t  const service=projectService(db,cache);\n    10\t  router.add('GET','/projects/:projectId',(req,p)=>ok(service.detail(requireSession(db,req.token).id,p.projectId)));\n    11\t  router.add('PATCH','/projects/:projectId',(req,p)=>ok(service.update(requireSession(db,req.token).id,p.projectId,req.body)));\n    12\t  router.add('GET','/organizations/:organizationId/projects',(req,p)=>ok(service.list(requireSession(db,req.token).id,p.organizationId,listOptions(req.query))));\n    13\t}\n=== src/seed.ts\n     1\timport type { Seed } from './db/database.ts';\n     2\texport function sampleSeed():Seed {return {\n     3\t  users:[{id:'alice',name:'Alice'},{id:'bob',name:'Bob'},{id:'both',name:'Both'}],\n     4\t  organizations:[{id:'org-a',name:'A'},{id:'org-b',name:'B'}],\n     5\t  memberships:[{userId:'alice',organizationId:'org-a'},{userId:'bob',organizationId:'org-b'},{userId:'both',organizationId:'org-a'},{userId:'both',organizationId:'org-b'}],\n     6\t  sessions:{alice:'alice',bob:'bob',both:'both'},\n     7\t  projects:[{id:'a1',organizationId:'org-a',name:'Alpha',updatedAt:3},{id:'a2',organizationId:'org-a',name:'Delta',updatedAt:1},{id:'a3',organizationId:'org-a',name:'Gamma',updatedAt:2},{id:'b1',organizationId:'org-b',name:'Beta',updatedAt:7},{id:'b2',organizationId:'org-b',name:'Echo',updatedAt:5},{id:'b3',organizationId:'org-b',name:'Foxtrot',updatedAt:6}],\n     8\t};}\n=== src/services/organization-service.ts\n     1\timport type { Database } from '../db/database.ts';\n     2\timport { membershipRepository } from '../db/membership-repository.ts';\n     3\timport { requireMembership } from '../auth/membership.ts';\n     4\timport { HttpError } from '../http/response.ts';\n     5\texport function organizationService(db:Database){return {\n     6\t  list(userId:string){return {items:membershipRepository(db).organizationsFor(userId)};},\n     7\t  detail(userId:string,id:string){requireMembership(db,userId,id);const org=db.organizations.get(id);if(!org)throw new HttpError(404,'not_found');return {...org};},\n     8\t};}\n=== src/services/project-service.ts\n     1\timport type { Database } from '../db/database.ts';\n     2\timport type { Cache } from '../cache/project-cache.ts';\n     3\timport type { ListOptions } from '../types.ts';\n     4\timport { projectRepository } from '../db/project-repository.ts';\n     5\timport { requireMembership } from '../auth/membership.ts';\n     6\timport { projectListKey, projectDetailKey } from '../cache/keys.ts';\n     7\timport { HttpError } from '../http/response.ts';\n     8\texport function projectService(db:Database,cache:Cache) {\n     9\t  const projects=projectRepository(db);\n    10\t  function detail(userId:string,projectId:string) {\n    11\t    const project=projects.find(projectId);\n    12\t    if(!project)throw new HttpError(404,'not_found');\n    13\t    return project;\n    14\t  }\n    15\t  return {\n    16\t    detail,\n    17\t    list(userId:string,organizationId:string,options:ListOptions) {\n    18\t      requireMembership(db,userId,organizationId);\n    19\t      const key=projectListKey(organizationId,options);\n    20\t      const cached=cache.get(key);\n    21\t      if(cached!==undefined)return cached;\n    22\t      const result=projects.list(organizationId,options);cache.set(key,result);return result;\n    23\t    },\n    24\t    update(userId:string,projectId:string,body:unknown) {\n    25\t      detail(userId,projectId);\n    26\t      if(!body||typeof body!=='object'||typeof (body as any).name!=='string'||!(body as any).name.trim())throw new HttpError(400,'invalid_body');\n    27\t      const updated=projects.update(projectId,(body as any).name.trim())!;\n    28\t      cache.delete(projectDetailKey(projectId));\n    29\t      return updated;\n    30\t    },\n    31\t  };\n    32\t}\n=== src/types.ts\n     1\texport type Project = { id: string; organizationId: string; name: string; updatedAt: number };\n     2\texport type Organization = { id: string; name: string };\n     3\texport type User = { id: string; name: string };\n     4\texport type ListOptions = { page: number; pageSize: number; sort: 'name' | 'updatedAt'; direction: 'asc' | 'desc' };\n     5\texport type Request = { method: string; path: string; token?: string; query?: Record<string,string>; body?: unknown };\n     6\texport type Response = { status: number; body: unknown };\n=== tests/account.test.ts\n     1\timport test from 'node:test';\n     2\timport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n     3\timport { createApp } from '../src/app.ts';\n     4\timport { sampleSeed } from '../src/seed.ts';\n     5\ttest('health and profile',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());assert.deepEqual(a.request({method:'GET',path:'/health'}).body,{status:'ok'});assert.equal((a.request({method:'GET',path:'/me',token:'alice'}).body as any).id,'alice');});\n     6\ttest('organizations scoped to user',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());assert.deepEqual((a.request({method:'GET',path:'/organizations',token:'alice'}).body as any).items.map((o:any)=>o.id),['org-a']);});\n     7\ttest('logout revokes session',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());assert.equal(a.request({method:'DELETE',path:'/session',token:'alice'}).status,204);assert.equal(a.request({method:'GET',path:'/me',token:'alice'}).status,401);});\n=== tests/projects.test.ts\n     1\timport test from 'node:test';\n     2\timport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n     3\timport { createApp } from '../src/app.ts';\n     4\timport { sampleSeed } from '../src/seed.ts';\n     5\ttest('authenticated detail',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());assert.equal(a.request({method:'GET',path:'/projects/a1',token:'alice'}).status,200);});\n     6\ttest('authenticated list',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());const r=a.request({method:'GET',path:'/organizations/org-a/projects',token:'alice'});assert.equal(r.status,200);assert.equal((r.body as any).items.length,3);});\n     7\ttest('update then read',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());assert.equal(a.request({method:'PATCH',path:'/projects/a1',token:'alice',body:{name:'New'}}).status,200);assert.equal((a.request({method:'GET',path:'/projects/a1',token:'alice'}).body as any).name,'New');});\n     8\ttest('anonymous request rejected',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());assert.deepEqual(a.request({method:'GET',path:'/projects/a1'}),{status:401,body:{error:'unauthorized'}});});\n     9\ttest('invalid update rejected',()=>{const a=createApp(sampleSeed());assert.equal(a.request({method:'PATCH',path:'/projects/a1',token:'alice',body:{name:''}}).status,400);});","stderr